00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.560
In our last episode, we covered
why Spanner is a great option

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.990
to hit the optimal balance
between scalability,

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:42.710
consistency, and high
availability for your database.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.440
In this episode, we're
going to connect the dots

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.530
to show you how Spanner is being
used to solve pressing problems

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:52.220
in financial services,
retail, and gaming.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:55.010
First up, financial services.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:58.040
Banks, fintech companies,
and their regulators

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.220
demand 24/7 access to
accurate information

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.980
in order to drive
core operations.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.840
They use Spanner in a wide
range of applications,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.040
including payment gateways
and online banking.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.810
Payment gateways
connect purchases

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.300
from many, often
millions of customers

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.190
to thousands of vendors.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:19.970
The scale alone can make
typical databases buckle.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.220
Compounding the problem,
all of this data

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:25.700
needs to be 100%
consistent as payments flow

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:29.390
through sophisticated anti-fraud
and settlement processes.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:31.550
Dropping a payment
or double counting

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:33.590
would be a serious issue.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:36.140
Spanner is also used
today in online banking

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.780
to improve reliability
and enable innovation

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.470
for mission-critical processes,
such as transaction tracking

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:44.870
and user profile management.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.670
Customer demands
for new products

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.590
and modern interactive
experiences

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:51.950
have taxed online
banks' databases.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.770
With last generation
scale-up technologies,

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.960
banks had to rearchitect
their systems

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.500
to scale in ways their
databases weren't designed for.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:04.040
The result is extra
complexity and maintenance.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:07.250
Developers have to work around
a fragmented view of the data,

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.620
while operators struggle
to ensure uptime

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.210
in a stitched together system.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.480
Banks and fintech
innovators choose

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.940
Spanner because of its
industry-leading five

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:21.020
nines of availability, zero plan
maintenance downtime, security

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.320
certifications, and the
highest consistency guarantees

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.270
of any scale-out database.

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:28.280
Spanner allows
financial services

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.380
to scale their
databases regionally

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:34.170
or even globally without
any downtime or compromises

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.160
to the integrity or
security of their data.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.110
This scale insurance
means they're

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:41.690
able to easily accommodate
long-term growth

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:45.320
or unexpected spikes without
painful rearchitecture

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.880
or downtime.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:50.000
Spanner eliminates complexity
and maintenance overhead

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.550
by pushing sharding
and replication down

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.460
into the database, not
as an afterthought.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.830
To your developers
and DBAs, it looks

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.820
like a single database instance
that can scale on-demand.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.820
Spanner is also used in
the red hot gaming industry

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.970
to support real-time gameplay
and in-game purchases that

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.250
are driving revenues.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.790
Popular game launches have
become cultural touchstones.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.180
Even a niche game can attract
millions of global users

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:21.830
at launch who demand interactive
gameplay that's always online.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:24.410
This burst of high
volume real-time traffic

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:27.860
can be game over for
common databases.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.840
Ensuring play from
a gamer in Asia

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.670
is immediately visible
to her opponent

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.890
in South America typically
requires manual database

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.410
sharding in order to scale.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.500
In modern digital games,
database maintenance windows

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.270
are also a big risk.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:45.520
With global players and
multiple game franchises,

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:47.760
it can be impossible
to schedule downtime

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.190
to patch the database
or updated schema

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.470
to support new capabilities.

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:55.890
For gaming or any other
always-on global business,

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:58.020
Spanner is fully
managed and never

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:01.440
needs to be paused for
patches, backups, failover,

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.900
or even schema updates.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.120
Using Google's dedicated
infrastructure,

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.930
Spanner guarantees consistency
and zero plan downtime,

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:12.420
even at the most
extreme scale, which

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:16.500
translates into better gameplay
and satisfied customers.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.890
Retailers face many of the same
challenges as banks and game

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.300
studios.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.610
New digital channels,
like online shopping

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.940
with in-store pickup, digital
wallet, and mobile rewards

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.260
redemption present
new opportunities,

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:32.400
but also impose additional
hurdles for already stretched

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.710
IT organizations.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.750
Retail supply chains
have also become

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.720
more complex and on-demand.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.960
Just in time fulfillment and
dynamic pricing and e-commerce

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:46.650
mean that a retailer's inventory
and product catalog must always

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:49.140
be up to date and consistent.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.450
Stock-outs erode
trust from consumers

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:55.650
whose alternative purchasing
options are on the rise.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.140
Spanner gives retailers
a consistent view

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:01.590
of their inventory, pricing,
and demand across channels

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:05.550
and locations without having
to hack together data stores

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:08.820
and using the SQL that
developers and analysts already

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:09.690
know.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:12.720
Online orders are immediately
reflected in inventory

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:16.440
across online and brick and
mortar stores and warehouses,

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:20.400
across thousands of products
and hundreds of locations.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.140
If this weren't
challenging enough,

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:25.170
retail often experiences
extreme seasonal spikes,

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.330
like during Black Friday.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:30.330
In the past, retailers
overprovisioned hardware

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:33.330
to handle holiday peaks,
but this is increasingly

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:36.030
expensive and inefficient.

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:38.220
Scaling on last
generation's databases

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:42.360
requires large upfront
expenses and downtime.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.940
New SQL technologies
claim web scale

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.880
but don't generally support
the transactions or SQL

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.200
that developers rely on.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.390
Spanner gives retailers
the confidence

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:54.520
that they'll be able
to handle peak periods

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.540
without large upfront costs
or maintenance overhead.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:02.110
Elastic scaling allows them to
expand regionally or globally

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:04.030
in a single click.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:07.360
Later, they can scale back down,
paying for only what they use,

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.310
without missing a beat.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:12.910
So there you have it, a dip into
the benefits of availability,

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:18.160
consistency, and scalability in
fin serve, gaming, and retail.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.880
High availability means you get
an industry-leading five nines

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:26.500
uptime and never have to work
around plan maintenance again.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:29.860
Get the strictest level of
consistency of any distributed

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.740
database without
sacrificing scalability

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.440
for operational workloads.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:38.110
And scale out and
back in as needed

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:41.230
to avoid costly excess
capacity while handling

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.030
unpredictability.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:46.750
This video is just a sampling
of the many industries and use

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:49.420
cases where Spanner helps
companies solve problems

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:51.890
and grow their business.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.590
So if you're curious
to learn more,

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.090
follow the links
in the description

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.680
below for additional
information.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.470
Thanks for joining
us today and stay

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:03.040
